ucture-as-Code: AWS CDK (TypeScript) – deploys VPC, Aurora, API Gateway, Lambda, S3, CloudFront, WAF, Cognito, IAM, etc.\\\\\\\\n   • Pipeline (AWS CodePipeline):\\\\\\\\n       – Source stage: pull request triggers build.\\\\\\\\n       – Build/Test stage:\\\\\\\\n           ∘ CodeBuild job #1: run frontend tests (Jest/Playwright) & create production build.\\\\\\\\n           ∘ CodeBuild job #2: run backend unit tests (pytest/jest), SAM/Serverless framework packaging.\\\\\\\\n           ∘ CodeBuild job #3: synth CDK & run `cdk diff` to ensure drift detection.\\\\\\\\n       – Deploy stage (manual approval gate for prod):\\\\\\\\n           ∘ CDK deploy via CodeBuild assumes dedicated deploy role.\\\\\\\\n           ∘ Upload frontend build artifacts to versioned S3 bucket, then trigger CloudFront invalidation.\\\\\\\\n           ∘ Deploy/rollback Lambda & API Gateway via SAM.\\\\\\\\n   • Release branches flow: feature ➜ develop ➜ staging ➜ main(production); each branch maps to target AWS account via cross-account CodePipeline.\\\\\\\\n   • Rollback: CodePipeline keeps last successful artifacts, one-click rollback; Aurora automatic backups, CloudFront versioned.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCost Optimisation Points\\\\\\\\n   • Serverless (Lambda, Aurora Serverless) means pay-per-use vs. always-on instances.\\\\\\\\n   • S3 + CloudFront for static assets is the lowest-cost, highest-performance combo.\\\\\\\\n   • Use Graviton2/3 arm64 Lambda runtime for 20–34 % cost reduction.\\\\\\\\n   • Set Aurora capacity min=0.5 ACU; auto-pause for off-peak HOA traffic.\\\\\\\\n   • Use Savings Plans for predictable Lambda/Build usage if traffic grows.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nSecurity Best Practices\\\\\\\\n   • OWASP automated scans in CodeBuild.\\\\\\\\n   • AWS Config + Security Hub for continuous compliance.\\\\\\\\n   • Centralized CloudTrail & GuardDuty.\\\\\\\\n   • Mandatory TLS 1.2+, HSTS via CloudFront.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis plan provides a fully-serverless, automatically scaling stack 