onal Setup (Infrastructure & Backend)**\\\\n1.  **Infrastructure:** Provision the core AWS environment using AWS CDK.\\\\n    - Create a new VPC with public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones.\\\\n    - Deploy the Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 PostgreSQL database into private subnets.\\\\n    - Set up AWS Secrets Manager for storing database credentials.\\\\n    - Configure initial IAM roles and policies with least-privilege access.\\\\n2.  **Backend:** Develop the core application and authentication.\\\\n    - Initialize the NestJS project with all required dependencies.\\\\n    - Establish the Prisma schema for `User` and other core models.\\\\n    - Implement the secure, invite-only user registration flow.\\\\n    - Implement the JWT-based login/logout/refresh endpoints.\\\\n    - Create Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) guards (`resident`, `admin`).\\\\n\\\\n**Phase 2: Content & Frontend Shell (Content Management & Frontend)**\\\\n1.  **Content Management:** Deploy and configure the Strapi CMS.\\\\n    - Provision a small, cost-effective host for the Strapi Docker container.\\\\n    - Define the 'News & Events' content type within the Strapi admin panel.\\\\n    - Configure public API access for published content.\\\\n    - Set up a webhook to be triggered upon content changes.\\\\n2.  **Frontend:** Initialize the project and build the main user interface structure.\\\\n    - Initialize the React project using Vite.\\\\n    - Build the primary `AppShell` component (Header, Footer, Navigation).\\\\n    - Implement client-side routing using React Router, including `AuthGuard` components for protected routes.\\\\n    - Connect the frontend to the backend's authentication endpoints (Login, Logout). Implement global state management for user authentication status.\\\\n\\\\n**Phase 3: Feature Implementation & Integration (All Teams)**\\\\n1.  **Backend:** Build out all required API endpoints as defined in the plan (e.g., for documents, user profiles, etc.).\\\\n2.  **Frontend:** Build all individual pages.\\\\n    - **Public Pages:** 'Contact Us', 'Bylaws', 'Schools'. Fetch data from the backend API where necessary.\\\\n    - **Protected Pages:** 'Dues', 'Annual Meetings'. These pages will be wrapped by the `AuthGuard`.\\\\n    - **News & Events Page:** Fetch and display content from the Strapi API.\\\\n3.  **Integration:** Connect all frontend components to their corresponding backend and Strapi API endpoints.\\\\n\\\\n**Phase 4: Deployment, Testing & Handoff**\\\\n1.  **Infrastructure:** Finalize and deploy the full CI/CD pipeline in AWS CodePipeline.\\\\n    - The pipeline will automatically test and deploy the backend to AWS Lambda and the frontend to S3/CloudFront.\\\\n    - Configure the production API Gateway to use a Lambda authorizer for validating JWTs from the backend.\\\\n2.  **Testing:** Conduct comprehensive end-to-end testing of all user flows, including registration, login, accessing protected content, and form submissions.\\\\n3.  **Handoff:** Create a simple user guide for the non-technical administrator on how to use the Strapi CMS to add and update 'News & Events' articles. Deliver the final, deployed website.\\\"\\n}\\n###<20240725_1819_Store_DEP>###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T18:19:04.831Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"<20240725_1819_Store_DEP>\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Document successfully stored. Your unique storage ID is: DOC-000001\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-25T18:19:04.831Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"The Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) is now co